{
  "_readme": "THE PROOF REGISTRY. A collector's live state is DERIVED from these records and is no longer declared beside the collector. Without a record a collector is `none`, whatever anybody believes about it.\n\nThe direction is the whole point: a real execution produces a record, the record is validated, and the state follows. Never a state written first and a record produced to agree with it.\n\nNO TENANT DATA REACHES THIS FILE. No hostname, no tenant identifier, no user principal name, no resource name, and no evidence content. A population is a count or a shape, never a list.",
  "_on_the_digest": "`artifact_digest` proves CONTINUITY with the artefact observed at that moment. It does not permit revalidating an artefact that no longer exists, and every record here carries `artifact_disposition` saying so plainly. A digest whose artefact was deleted under the tenant-data rule is a fingerprint of something nobody can produce again, and claiming more for it would be the same overreach this registry exists to remove.",
