  "_on_stages": "A RUN PROVES SEVERAL DIFFERENT THINGS AND THEY ARE NOT ONE THING. `acquisition` is the Microsoft surface actually read; `evidence` is the document produced from it; `assessment` is rules consuming that evidence; `bundle` is the canonical artefact; `consumer` is somebody independent opening it.\n\n`bundle` and `consumer` read `not-attempted` on every migrated record because the matrix they were transcribed from does not mention either. That is not a gap to be filled in from memory. Nobody wrote it down, so nothing is proved, and the ladder says so rather than rounding up.\n\n`not-applicable` is the stage not existing here: a collector that feeds no rule has no assessment to prove, and demanding one would make the top of the ladder unreachable for a capability that is complete."
